    "https://stevenson.peopleadmin.com/postings/11322": {
      "title": "Full-Time Faculty, Clinical Psychology (Open Rank)",
      "description": "Stevenson University Applicant Portal | Full-Time Faculty, Clinical Psychology (Open Rank) Skip to Main Content Find Your Role: We strive to achieve an environment and an atmosphere that supports, challenges, and inspires every individual on campus. Learn how the Stevenson Way makes this effort possible and how you can become part of a great place to work. Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Full-Time Faculty, Clinical Psychology (Open Rank) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Description Posting Number 201201547P Position Title Full-Time Faculty, Clinical Psychology (Open Rank) Department Academic Affairs: Psy.D. in Clinical Psychology Position Summary The Full-Time Faculty, Clinical Psychology is a 10-month full-time faculty appointment in the Psy.D. Program in Clinical Psychology. As a core faculty member of the Psy.D. program, the primary responsibilities include teaching, dissertation supervision and committee work, student advising and mentoring, service to the department and university, and continued scholarship in the field as defined in the Stevenson University policies and the Psy.D. in Clinical Psychology Full-Time Faculty Job Description. Teaching responsibilities include 24 contact hours per academic year. Additional responsibilities include, but are not limited to, student recruitment, retention, and placement efforts (which may include occasional off-campus, evening, or weekend duties/activities), and participating in the life of the university. Rank and title will be determined at the time of hiring and will be commensurate with education and experience. Education/Experience Doctoral degree from an APA -accredited program in a health service psychology area (i.e., clinical, counseling, or school) required with graduate teaching experience in psychology and experience in clinical practice preferred. Teaching, clinical, and research specialty areas are open; clinical and teaching competencies in the areas of psychological assessment, research methods, statistics, ethics, human development, and/or working with children and adolescents are preferred. Must hold an active psychology license in Maryland or a neighboring jurisdiction or be license-eligible at time of hire. Knowledge/Skills/Ability Demonstrated knowledge and expertise in the teaching of psychology at the graduate level. Demonstrated expertise in clinical practice. Commitment to advising, mentoring and guiding students and supervising student scholarly activity, including doctoral dissertation research. Ability to work with students from diverse backgrounds and practice inclusive pedagogy. Demonstrated student-centered approach to teaching, and a commitment to student achievement. Demonstrated ability to engage in curriculum development, planning, implementation, and assessment. Ability to assess student performance and learning. Knowledge of state and national training and licensure requirements and APA / APPIC standards in teaching and supervising doctoral students preferred. Ability to work effectively with colleagues in the department and the University. Demonstrated ability to communicate effectively verbally and in writing with students, peers, and professional contacts. Commitment to Stevenson’s values of integrity, excellence, learning, and community. Commitment to professional development. Proficient in Microsoft applications, including PowerPoint, Word, and Excel. Proficient with quantitative and/or qualitative data analysis programs. Excellent technology and organizational skills and experience working with Blackboard or a similar platform. Ability to travel between campuses. Ability to work occasional evenings and weekends. Physical Requirements Light work: Exerting up to 20 pounds of force occasionally and/or a negligible amount of force constantly to move objects. Sitting, standing, walking, talking, hearing, keyboarding, and repetitive motions. Close visual acuity. Position requires sitting and standing for extended periods of time and the ability to speak clearly and effectively for an extended period of time. Essential Functions Instructional Activity Engage in instructional activity (teaching and serving as dissertation chair) totaling 24 contact hours per academic year. Maintain and improve competence in subjects taught; Prepare courses and teaching materials (including syllabi) in accordance with published faculty workload guidelines; Grade all student work in a timely manner; Hold office hours (minimum of 3 hours per week); Meet with students as needed as it relates to instructional activity. Evaluate, update, and revise courses regularly. Dissertation chair responsibilities include regularly meeting with students to discuss relevant literature, study methods, data analysis, and implications; reviewing and giving feedback on manuscripts, IRB applications, and other relevant materials; and participating in proposal and final defense meetings. Advise Psy.D. students in academic, research, and career matters. Serve on student dissertation committees as requested or assigned. Committee member responsibilities include reading and providing feedback on manuscripts and study materials; participating in defense meetings; and consulting throughout the dissertation process on aspects of the dissertation in which they have relevant expertise as needed. Participate in the development, administration, and grading of comprehensive examinations. Participate in the assessment activities of the Department, School, and University. Alert the Graduate Program Director and/or other appropriate university personnel to student concerns on a timely basis. Scholarly Activity Maintain independent pursuits-including scholarly or applied projects-to enhance teaching effectiveness. Attend professional conferences, workshops, or meetings to maintain currency in an area of academic interest. Maintain scholarly activities that contribute to the profession through publications or presentations at regional or national conferences. Seek external funding to support scholarly or programmatic activities as appropriate. Maintain active clinical psychology license in Maryland or jurisdiction of residence/practice. Service Activity Attend all faculty, staff, University, and Psy.D. Program meetings, including contractually mandated recruitment activities. Review application materials for and interview prospective students. Participate in Psy.D. Program events and attend all required milestone events, including commencement exercises. Serve on Psy.D. Program and/or University committees. Participate in professional peer review and ongoing departmental activities, such as curriculum assessment and accreditation-related activities. Perform professional service to the community, including psychology practice and other uses of academic and professional expertise to serve the profession of psychology and the University. Demonstrate collegiality, as well as professional and ethical conduct, that enhances teaching, learning, and the general reputation of all persons in the academy. Reports To Program Director, Clinical Psychology Quick Link for Posting https://stevenson.peopleadmin.com/postings/11213 Posting Information Number of Available Positions 1 Work Location Greenspring Position Category Faculty Position Type Full-time Faculty Months/Year 10 Hrs/Week 40 Hrs/Year 1733 If scheduled to work less than 12 months, beginning date Ending Date FLSA Exempt Payroll Monthly Hiring Salary Range Anticipated to be $77,000 - $85,000 Benefits https://www.stevenson.edu/human-resources/benefits/ Recruitment Instructions Open to All Applicants Posting Date 08/04/2026 Closing Date/Application Deadline Open Until Filled No EEO Statement We are an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability status, protected veteran status, genetics, or any other characteristic protected by law. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter/Letter of Application Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents Stevenson University Main Campus 100 Campus Circle Owings Mills, MD, 21117-7804 1-877-468-6852 410-486-7001 Greenspring Campus 1525 Greenspring Valley Road Stevenson, MD, 21153-064 Maps & Directions Campus Map Join the Conversation Facebook Twitter Instagram YouTube LinkedIn Flickr Campus Resources News & Events Directory Campus Security & Parking SU Alert Employment SU Now Portal Mustang Athletics Give to Stevenson Stevenson University © 2017 Stevenson University Title IX Annual Security & Fire Safety Report Consumer Information Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
